  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 311 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nLabor Day Weekend...East/northeast low-level winds from high \npressure over Ontario and the Great Lakes has allowed for a shallow \nlayer of low-level moisture and clouds to prevail across much of the \nregion throughout the morning and into this afternoon. Anticipate \nthese clouds to gradually dissipate by this evening with the loss of \ndaytime heating. Skies will be mostly clear overnight, with the \npotential for patchy fog to develop early Sunday morning. Expect dry \nconditions and above normal temperatures (highs ranging from the \nupper 70s to low 80s) to continue through the remainder of the Labor \nDay weekend as the high pressure and upper-level ridging remain in \nplace. Patchy fog may develop late Sunday night into Monday morning \nas well.\n\nRest of the forecast...The ridge and high pressure will gradually \ndepart late Monday as return flow sets up ahead of an approaching \nsystem/weak cold front progged to move over the area late Monday \nthrough early Wednesday morning. It is too early to determine the \nsevere potential, but this pattern would favor strong/severe storms \nif the storms move through during peak heating on Tuesday. Will \ncontinue to monitor over the coming days. Mainly dry conditions \nreturn for the remainder of Wednesday through early Friday.",
